1
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:02,160
You mean her truth?

2
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:03,920
The woman who tore our family apart?!

3
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:06,120
Neen didn't tear our family apart.

4
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:08,240
I know a way you can earn money.

5
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:15,880
The investigators

6
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:18,880
can't charge her
with solicitation of kidnapping.

7
00:01:18,960 --> 00:01:20,440
Just because she isn't charged

8
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:22,840
doesn't mean she isn't guilty.

9
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:24,720
You want me to go to jail that bad?

10
00:01:24,800 --> 00:01:28,240
At least
it will stop you from hurting others,

11
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:29,480
especially our daughter!

12
00:01:29,560 --> 00:01:30,960
Sooner or later,

13
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:33,440
she'll get her karma
for what she did to us.

14
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:34,680
You reap

15
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:36,880
<i>what you sow.</i>

16
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:49,920
Nat told me to wait for you in here.

17
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:04,760
Neen.

18
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:11,000
Wanna grab some coffee

19
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:14,240
at our spot?

20
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:23,040
Do you remember?

21
00:02:24,520 --> 00:02:25,760
This place

22
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:28,360
is where we first met.

23
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:34,640
I do.

24
00:02:35,920 --> 00:02:37,120
I never forgot.

25
00:02:45,560 --> 00:02:47,640
This is where we started,

26
00:02:49,880 --> 00:02:51,800
so I wanted us to end things here.

27
00:03:07,080 --> 00:03:10,480
SIGNATURE - RUNCHLAPHAT TRIKITTIPHUM
SIGNATURE - PEERACHA PACHARATHAKUL

28
00:03:15,400 --> 00:03:16,760
I signed it already.

29
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:34,200
Thank you

30
00:03:35,320 --> 00:03:37,440
for all the days we were together.

31
00:03:42,800 --> 00:03:45,760
You always made me really happy.

32
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,640
You made me want to wake up early…

33
00:03:54,920 --> 00:03:56,920
just to see your face.

34
00:04:00,920 --> 00:04:02,880
You made me want to come home…

35
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:06,800
so I could wait for you.

36
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:11,760
I would always wonder if you were hungry…

37
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:14,760
or tired.

38
00:04:21,320 --> 00:04:24,080
You really gave me hope.

39
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:36,720
I wanted to thank you too.

40
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:42,880
Thank you for loving me so much

41
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:46,560
that I felt like…

42
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:50,160
I matter.

43
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,720
I never imagined

44
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:02,320
I could mean so much to someone.

45
00:05:20,640 --> 00:05:22,280
Neen.

46
00:05:27,680 --> 00:05:29,920
I want you to know that…

47
00:05:32,200 --> 00:05:34,480
no matter what our relationship is,

48
00:05:38,520 --> 00:05:42,000
you're the best part of my life.

49
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:03,480
Same here.

50
00:08:21,200 --> 00:08:24,040
TOULOUSE, FRANCE - 2 YEARS LATER

51
00:08:25,280 --> 00:08:27,760
Wow. What is Miss Neen doing this time?

52
00:08:27,840 --> 00:08:28,600
CEO GIRL SPOTTED
GETTING COZY WITH FAMOUS ACTRESS

53
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:30,480
She's opened a new restaurant.

54
00:08:31,560 --> 00:08:33,039
I thought it was about her dating someone.

55
00:08:35,799 --> 00:08:40,240
She's not a celebrity or a pop idol.
Why would she be in stories like that?

56
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:42,320
Oh, you're right.

57
00:08:42,400 --> 00:08:45,920
A rich girl like her should be dating
someone in showbiz.

58
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:49,280
Next time she's in the news,
it'll probably be her wedding.

59
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:55,480
You know, I never imagined
I'd get to be here either.

60
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:59,240
That's just how life is.
Nothing is certain.

61
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:00,840
Who knows?

62
00:09:00,920 --> 00:09:05,080
You might get back together with Neen
and end up remarrying.

63
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:11,440
If that ever happens, that'd be great.

64
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:16,240
You won't even consider
starting over with someone new?

65
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:21,360
Well, I still love her.

66
00:09:24,640 --> 00:09:26,320
I never stopped loving her.

67
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:39,080
- Were you on a date?
- Huh?

68
00:09:40,400 --> 00:09:42,960
I saw so many pictures
of you and that actress.

69
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:45,480
What date? We're just friends.

70
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:49,640
And here I thought
you were dating someone new.

71
00:09:50,880 --> 00:09:53,840
Who would I date?
You don't even date anyone either.

72
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:56,800
I don't date because I'm busy.

73
00:09:56,880 --> 00:09:59,560
But you know why you're not dating?

74
00:10:01,280 --> 00:10:04,640
Stop saying bad things about Runch,
or I'll get mad at you.

75
00:10:05,240 --> 00:10:07,320
You're always defending
your wife, aren't you?

76
00:10:07,920 --> 00:10:10,120
Oh. I mean, your ex-wife.

77
00:10:11,520 --> 00:10:15,280
So, where did you see the photos?

78
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:19,320
Well, everyone's sharing them online.
She's a famous actress too, right?

79
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:21,160
It's a big deal right now.

80
00:10:21,240 --> 00:10:23,800
Are you sure you're not interested?

81
00:10:25,560 --> 00:10:26,920
It's really nothing, right?

82
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:33,320
Well, she was hitting on me.
I already rejected her, though.

83
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:37,680
You would really reject a lead actress?

84
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:40,040
Stop taking a dig at Runch, will you?

85
00:10:40,120 --> 00:10:42,480
Okay. I guess
you're not over your darling.

86
00:10:42,560 --> 00:10:43,560
Nai!

87
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:46,160
I bet your darling
has seen the news by now

88
00:10:46,240 --> 00:10:51,360
that her ex-wife was seen
getting cozy with a lead actress.

89
00:10:51,440 --> 00:10:53,560
She probably doesn't
care about me anymore.

90
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:55,800
Who knows?

91
00:10:57,360 --> 00:10:58,360
What's gotten into you?

92
00:10:58,440 --> 00:11:00,720
You were the one
who wanted me to divorce her so badly.

93
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:06,200
I guess it's because I see now
that you cannot love anyone else,

94
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:08,360
if it's not that beautiful woman.

95
00:11:09,080 --> 00:11:12,200
Look, I don't have an issue
with being alone,

96
00:11:12,280 --> 00:11:14,520
nor am I incapable
of loving someone new. Got it?

97
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:16,360
Are you sure you don't have an issue?

98
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:19,960
You were still crying at a wedding
thinking of Runch, so I'm not too sure.

99
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,560
That Plengpin just
cannot keep a secret, can she?

100
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:27,280
Crying because you miss your ex-wife

101
00:11:28,360 --> 00:11:31,000
- is perfectly normal.
- Do you have an ex-wife too?

102
00:11:31,080 --> 00:11:34,160
No. And I don't want to either.

103
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:36,600
But if you don't want her
to be just an ex-wife,

104
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:41,240
you know what to do, right?
Or do I need to tell you?

105
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:46,760
No need. I'm not doing anything.
When it's over, it's over. For good.

106
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:49,240
We split up for good. It's over.

107
00:11:50,760 --> 00:11:53,400
- I'll wait and see.
- Fine. You'll see.

108
00:12:00,200 --> 00:12:04,560
1 MONTH LATER

109
00:12:11,160 --> 00:12:12,320
Neen!

110
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:15,160
- Oh. Hi, Dad.
- Hi.

111
00:12:15,240 --> 00:12:17,120
It's been a while.

112
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:19,720
Yes. How have you been?

113
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:22,240
I've been alright.
It's been a bit of a struggle.

114
00:12:22,320 --> 00:12:24,160
- Mostly okay.
- I see.

115
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:27,160
What are you up to around here today?

116
00:12:28,760 --> 00:12:30,280
I'm here to meet…

117
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:34,040
Oh. I'll get out of your hair, then.
If you'll excuse me.

118
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:35,680
- See you later.
- Alright.

119
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:54,240
- Hi, Dad.
- Hi, honey.

120
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:56,720
- When did you get here?
- About ten minutes ago.

121
00:12:56,800 --> 00:12:59,080
I already ordered some food.
Help yourself.

122
00:12:59,680 --> 00:13:02,560
Wow. Thank you.

123
00:13:02,640 --> 00:13:06,000
I just want Thai food today.
I really missed it.

124
00:13:06,080 --> 00:13:07,880
Anything will do.

125
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:17,920
- Runch.
- Yes?

126
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:20,040
I ran into Neen earlier.

127
00:13:20,120 --> 00:13:22,360
She was still calling me "Dad."

128
00:13:30,560 --> 00:13:33,520
How has Mom been doing?

129
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:36,680
She's a lot calmer now.

130
00:13:36,760 --> 00:13:40,000
She's probably realized
there's nothing she can do.

131
00:13:40,880 --> 00:13:45,200
They scammed me! Those low-life scammers!

132
00:13:45,280 --> 00:13:48,600
My life savings
and my retirement pay… All gone!

133
00:13:48,680 --> 00:13:51,000
Why throw a fit?
That won't earn your money back.

134
00:13:51,080 --> 00:13:52,480
What do you want me to do, then?!

135
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:59,000
Who would've known that bank teller
would turn out to be a scammer?

136
00:13:59,080 --> 00:14:01,800
What bank teller would call you
asking you to transfer money?

137
00:14:03,880 --> 00:14:08,080
I just wanted my money to grow.
I didn't do anything wrong.

138
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:09,160
Really?

139
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:11,760
There's news about people
getting scammed everywhere.

140
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:13,120
You really haven't seen it?

141
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:14,800
Are you blaming me?

142
00:14:14,880 --> 00:14:17,200
I'm not. I'm just telling the truth.

143
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:19,760
And you know what we have to do?
We have to sell the house.

144
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:22,840
Are you crazy? This is our house!

145
00:14:23,640 --> 00:14:24,920
If anything,

146
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,880
we should ask Runch for help.

147
00:14:26,960 --> 00:14:29,680
Did you already forget
what you did to her?

148
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:31,680
There's no way she'll help us.

149
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:35,280
You caused all these problems alone,
and you want her to take responsibility?

150
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:48,680
How do I live?

151
00:14:50,680 --> 00:14:52,880
Like a normal person,

152
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:54,800
something you never wanted to be.

153
00:14:56,440 --> 00:14:58,640
Or if there's nowhere left to turn to,

154
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:00,080
come join me at the temple.

155
00:15:00,640 --> 00:15:03,120
No, no!

156
00:15:07,280 --> 00:15:09,960
How am I supposed to live now?!

157
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:23,080
It's probably for the best.

158
00:15:24,560 --> 00:15:27,320
Otherwise, she'd still
be causing trouble non-stop.

159
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:29,320
Yeah.

160
00:15:30,760 --> 00:15:33,560
How long will you
be staying here this time?

161
00:15:33,640 --> 00:15:36,000
About a month.

162
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:40,480
Then after that, I'll be in France
for a while until I graduate.

163
00:15:42,160 --> 00:15:45,080
Will you go see Neen before then?

164
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:12,240
One americano, please.

165
00:16:12,960 --> 00:16:14,360
Oh! Hello, beautiful.

166
00:16:14,440 --> 00:16:15,800
Where have you been?

167
00:16:15,880 --> 00:16:17,520
Long time no see.

168
00:16:18,320 --> 00:16:20,160
Americano, as always, right?

169
00:16:20,240 --> 00:16:21,280
Yes, please.

170
00:16:22,800 --> 00:16:26,800
Oh. I thought you were here alone.
Your girlfriend came too?

171
00:16:46,720 --> 00:16:48,320
I missed you.

172
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:51,480
You're saying that right away, huh?

173
00:16:52,240 --> 00:16:53,440
Yes.

174
00:16:57,560 --> 00:17:00,800
At lunch, Dad told me he ran into you.

175
00:17:02,040 --> 00:17:04,920
Well? Were you hoping to run into me too?

176
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:05,839
Yes.

177
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:07,720
I was.

178
00:17:09,359 --> 00:17:11,520
You are way too honest, Runchlaphat.

179
00:17:22,359 --> 00:17:23,520
Going already?

180
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:26,920
Yeah.

181
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,720
Can I come with you?

182
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:31,560
You mean you need a ride?

183
00:17:31,640 --> 00:17:32,680
I mean,

184
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:34,640
I want to come with you.

185
00:17:35,600 --> 00:17:37,040
To your place.

186
00:17:42,080 --> 00:17:43,520
To stay the night with me?

187
00:17:46,040 --> 00:17:47,600
Can I?

188
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:54,760
Look, Gorgeous.

189
00:17:57,360 --> 00:17:58,880
Yes?

190
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:05,520
If we're going to do this,
we both need to be single.

191
00:18:06,480 --> 00:18:08,280
Well, I am.

192
00:18:09,480 --> 00:18:10,880
I always have been.

193
00:18:13,120 --> 00:18:14,600
Don't tell me…

194
00:18:16,320 --> 00:18:17,680
you're dating someone?

195
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:19,160
I'm also single.

196
00:18:26,760 --> 00:18:28,240
But are you sure you want to come?

197
00:18:45,800 --> 00:18:49,320
My parents and Nai are in the US.
No one's home.

198
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:51,520
You're home alone?

199
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:55,080
Yes.

200
00:18:59,120 --> 00:19:00,960
Do you need anything besides water?

201
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:02,400
No, thanks.

202
00:19:04,080 --> 00:19:07,560
Then let's shower.
I'll find you a pair of pajamas.

203
00:19:09,960 --> 00:19:12,040
Which room am I staying in?

204
00:19:12,840 --> 00:19:14,280
In another room.

205
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:22,680
Or did you want to be in my room?

206
00:19:25,240 --> 00:19:26,600
Can I?

207
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:32,240
Of course not. Don't be silly.

208
00:19:37,880 --> 00:19:39,920
Then any room will do.

209
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:45,080
Of course. Let's go.

210
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:48,080
Hold on.

211
00:19:51,360 --> 00:19:53,000
Can we sit down and talk first?

212
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:07,440
How have you been in the past two years?

213
00:20:09,840 --> 00:20:13,880
I've been alright.
I just work and go home every day.

214
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:16,280
In a loop. Nothing significant.

215
00:20:16,960 --> 00:20:18,200
What about you?

216
00:20:19,960 --> 00:20:24,520
I went to study in France
not long after we got divorced.

217
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:28,000
Over there,

218
00:20:28,080 --> 00:20:30,520
Natee helped me in so many ways.

219
00:20:33,440 --> 00:20:35,280
The classes are super hard.

220
00:20:35,920 --> 00:20:39,280
Sometimes, I wondered
why I even went in the first place.

221
00:20:40,520 --> 00:20:42,400
When do you graduate?

222
00:20:43,160 --> 00:20:45,560
I'm trying to graduate this year.

223
00:20:49,280 --> 00:20:50,480
So…

224
00:20:51,160 --> 00:20:52,920
will you be back?

225
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:57,480
Of course.

226
00:21:10,880 --> 00:21:12,760
Ever since the incident,

227
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:16,720
I never contacted my mother again.

228
00:21:20,440 --> 00:21:22,960
I cut her off financially too.

229
00:21:27,040 --> 00:21:29,560
She has no idea
where I am or what I'm doing.

230
00:21:40,280 --> 00:21:42,360
Is it tough over there in France?

231
00:21:49,160 --> 00:21:50,360
Of course.

232
00:21:54,560 --> 00:21:56,440
It was tough because I missed you.

233
00:21:59,160 --> 00:22:01,320
You'd better watch what you say.

234
00:22:01,400 --> 00:22:03,280
We already got divorced, Runch.

235
00:22:13,680 --> 00:22:15,320
I really did miss you, though.

236
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:22,440
Yes.

237
00:22:23,600 --> 00:22:25,440
I really missed you too.

238
00:22:37,240 --> 00:22:38,600
Can I kiss you?

239
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:42,840
You can do way more than that.

240
00:23:56,200 --> 00:23:58,480
Why are you up so early, Neen?

241
00:24:00,880 --> 00:24:04,440
I… I need to go to work.

242
00:24:07,520 --> 00:24:09,920
Call in sick and stay with me.

243
00:24:11,240 --> 00:24:15,040
This time, I'll be in France for a while.

244
00:24:16,640 --> 00:24:20,920
Stay with me. Please? Please?

245
00:24:21,000 --> 00:24:24,320
Runch… Don't do that.

246
00:24:26,960 --> 00:24:28,200
Why not?

247
00:24:29,280 --> 00:24:30,840
Am I making you blush?

248
00:24:31,520 --> 00:24:33,360
How could I not?

249
00:24:34,000 --> 00:24:35,560
It's been two whole years.

250
00:24:35,640 --> 00:24:38,960
We just saw each other again
and ended up in bed right away.

251
00:24:40,280 --> 00:24:42,200
This can't be right, Runch.

252
00:24:43,960 --> 00:24:45,400
You were drunk. That's why.

253
00:24:48,040 --> 00:24:50,200
I wasn't.

254
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:52,440
I was fully in control.

255
00:24:53,440 --> 00:24:54,760
I did it all on purpose.

256
00:24:59,280 --> 00:25:01,120
Please stay.

257
00:25:01,880 --> 00:25:05,400
I missed you so bad,
and I don't want to waste any time.

258
00:25:05,480 --> 00:25:08,360
Please, please, please?

259
00:25:08,440 --> 00:25:10,520
Quite smooth, aren't you?

260
00:25:12,920 --> 00:25:15,520
Only with you.

261
00:25:15,600 --> 00:25:17,200
So don't worry.

262
00:25:47,040 --> 00:25:49,760
I was so happy last night.

263
00:25:51,960 --> 00:25:54,400
Because you got to sleep with a girl?

264
00:25:56,200 --> 00:25:58,840
Because I got to sleep with you.

265
00:26:02,160 --> 00:26:04,680
I didn't tell you last night

266
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:07,200
that I…

267
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:09,080
still love you.

268
00:26:11,560 --> 00:26:13,000
I never stopped loving you.

269
00:26:14,080 --> 00:26:16,040
I've always loved you just the same.

270
00:26:19,480 --> 00:26:21,200
You're being all sweet. What do you want?

271
00:26:25,880 --> 00:26:28,240
If I told you

272
00:26:30,400 --> 00:26:32,520
I want you as my wife,

273
00:26:36,160 --> 00:26:37,640
would that be possible?

274
00:27:00,520 --> 00:27:04,640
I'm so glad
Dad hasn't sold this house yet,

275
00:27:05,720 --> 00:27:08,200
so we get to see each other every day.

276
00:27:11,240 --> 00:27:12,280
Yeah.

277
00:27:12,800 --> 00:27:17,720
But my parents are starting to wonder
why I'm staying here every night.

278
00:27:18,480 --> 00:27:20,840
So I told them,

279
00:27:20,920 --> 00:27:24,880
"Work's been busy,
and this house is closer to work."

280
00:27:24,960 --> 00:27:28,080
Well done. That's my good girl.

281
00:27:37,000 --> 00:27:38,200
Neen.

282
00:27:39,000 --> 00:27:40,400
Yes?

283
00:27:43,440 --> 00:27:44,840
Will you marry me?

284
00:27:51,840 --> 00:27:53,680
Isn't it too soon?

285
00:27:55,600 --> 00:27:57,800
I will make sure

286
00:27:59,080 --> 00:28:00,920
things are different this time

287
00:28:02,520 --> 00:28:03,880
when we get married again.

288
00:28:05,520 --> 00:28:07,680
I promise it won't be the same.

289
00:28:12,600 --> 00:28:14,240
But if you don't want that…

290
00:28:17,160 --> 00:28:19,240
will you be my girlfriend first?

291
00:28:21,560 --> 00:28:23,200
Will it be weird?

292
00:28:24,320 --> 00:28:26,120
To date again

293
00:28:26,200 --> 00:28:28,080
all of a sudden?

294
00:28:30,800 --> 00:28:32,360
It won't be.

295
00:28:34,920 --> 00:28:38,680
You'll be studying abroad anyway,
so what's the hurry?

296
00:28:39,480 --> 00:28:41,480
I will graduate as soon as I can

297
00:28:42,080 --> 00:28:43,440
so I can come back.

298
00:28:46,160 --> 00:28:48,280
If I say yes now,

299
00:28:48,360 --> 00:28:51,600
we'll be in
a long-distance relationship, right?

300
00:28:52,920 --> 00:28:54,880
- Then sure.
- What?

301
00:28:54,960 --> 00:28:56,600
I'm saying yes.

302
00:28:58,640 --> 00:29:01,160
Just don't date anyone while you're there.

303
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:02,440
I won't.

304
00:29:03,680 --> 00:29:06,880
Are you happy now that
I'm your girlfriend again?

305
00:29:07,840 --> 00:29:09,400
Of course I am.

306
00:29:10,320 --> 00:29:12,520
I'm over the moon.

307
00:29:12,600 --> 00:29:14,880
I used to be your wife, you know.

308
00:29:15,800 --> 00:29:18,400
Well, if we marry again,

309
00:29:19,400 --> 00:29:22,080
I'll be so happy I'll cry.

310
00:29:49,480 --> 00:29:53,680
What's so great about France?
You've been flying there every month.

311
00:29:53,760 --> 00:29:55,200
Answer me.

312
00:29:55,280 --> 00:29:58,520
Well, maybe I just want to travel.

313
00:29:58,600 --> 00:30:01,200
Why would you travel every month?

314
00:30:01,800 --> 00:30:04,720
Don't tell me you found a new girlfriend.

315
00:30:04,800 --> 00:30:07,200
- A French woman? How did you two meet?
- No.

316
00:30:07,280 --> 00:30:08,800
Calm down.

317
00:30:08,880 --> 00:30:10,520
I don't have a new girlfriend.

318
00:30:10,600 --> 00:30:11,680
Well?

319
00:30:11,760 --> 00:30:12,960
It's my ex.

320
00:30:14,280 --> 00:30:16,320
- Oh my god!
- My god! Since when?

321
00:30:16,400 --> 00:30:17,360
But how?

322
00:30:17,440 --> 00:30:18,400
What happened?

323
00:30:18,480 --> 00:30:22,880
We just so happened
to run into each other, and…

324
00:30:22,960 --> 00:30:26,040
And? And you two ended up in bed, I bet.

325
00:30:27,720 --> 00:30:29,640
Alright, Ms. Know-It-All.

326
00:30:29,720 --> 00:30:30,800
Hold on.

327
00:30:30,880 --> 00:30:33,000
Your new girlfriend is your ex-wife?

328
00:30:35,680 --> 00:30:38,280
Wow. You must really like her.

329
00:30:38,360 --> 00:30:39,600
- Stop teasing me.
- I see a smile.

330
00:30:39,680 --> 00:30:41,640
Does it still feel the same?

331
00:30:41,720 --> 00:30:44,880
Like when you were hitting on her,
and when you started dating?

332
00:30:49,600 --> 00:30:53,080
Well, it feels the same sometimes.

333
00:30:53,840 --> 00:30:55,360
She's changed a little.

334
00:30:55,440 --> 00:30:57,600
But in a good way.

335
00:30:58,200 --> 00:31:00,560
And will you get married again?

336
00:31:01,320 --> 00:31:02,360
I don't know.

337
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:07,400
I've gotten married
and registered my marriage before.

338
00:31:07,480 --> 00:31:12,200
And none of that could guarantee
that Runch and I would last.

339
00:31:12,280 --> 00:31:13,480
Yeah.

340
00:31:14,680 --> 00:31:16,800
Anyway, we'll see about that.

341
00:31:17,320 --> 00:31:18,240
I understand.

342
00:31:18,320 --> 00:31:20,840
Still, we're happy to hear

343
00:31:20,920 --> 00:31:22,400
you gave her a second chance,

344
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:24,600
and yourself too.

345
00:31:24,680 --> 00:31:26,480
It'll definitely be better this time.

346
00:31:28,400 --> 00:31:29,560
Well, I hope so.

347
00:31:41,280 --> 00:31:42,360
Neen!

348
00:31:49,520 --> 00:31:50,440
Come here.

349
00:31:55,440 --> 00:31:58,200
Wait, wait. Calm down, Neen.

350
00:31:58,280 --> 00:32:01,440
No way. I missed you. I missed you so bad.

351
00:32:01,520 --> 00:32:05,200
I kept wishing there was a portal
leading straight to your room.

352
00:32:05,280 --> 00:32:07,520
I'm tired of flying for several hours.

353
00:32:08,360 --> 00:32:10,440
Relax, Neen.

354
00:32:11,080 --> 00:32:13,440
I was hoping to take you out for a walk.

355
00:32:13,520 --> 00:32:15,080
There's a new café in town.

356
00:32:15,160 --> 00:32:18,240
It just opened
after you flew back last month.

357
00:32:20,360 --> 00:32:21,600
Neen, honey…

358
00:32:21,680 --> 00:32:22,680
Yes?

359
00:32:23,200 --> 00:32:25,760
How about we go out after an hour?

360
00:32:26,560 --> 00:32:28,280
You sure that's enough?

361
00:32:28,360 --> 00:32:30,720
I guess more than an hour is fine.

362
00:32:40,800 --> 00:32:43,160
I missed you so much.

363
00:33:07,080 --> 00:33:07,920
Let me see that.

364
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:11,720
You know, I really love oranges.
Let me see that one too.

365
00:33:11,800 --> 00:33:13,960
Orange cheeks!

366
00:33:15,800 --> 00:33:18,360
Actually, let's not buy those yet.

367
00:33:18,440 --> 00:33:20,720
Yeah, they're heavy. Let's buy them later.

368
00:33:30,120 --> 00:33:31,200
I'll buy…

369
00:33:31,720 --> 00:33:33,600
this one.

370
00:33:34,640 --> 00:33:36,880
- How much is this?
- Five euros.

371
00:33:38,400 --> 00:33:39,320
Thank you.

372
00:33:44,120 --> 00:33:45,520
This is for you.

373
00:33:49,960 --> 00:33:52,640
- Thank you, baby.
- For you.

374
00:34:27,920 --> 00:34:29,800
- Let me have a bite.
- Here.

375
00:34:32,760 --> 00:34:33,639
All yours.

376
00:34:44,719 --> 00:34:50,480
3 YEARS LATER

377
00:34:53,320 --> 00:34:55,840
Hello, Professor Runchlaphat.

378
00:34:55,920 --> 00:34:58,440
What time does your class finish today?

379
00:34:58,520 --> 00:35:01,400
<i>At five. Why?</i>

380
00:35:01,480 --> 00:35:04,120
Nothing. I was just wondering.

381
00:35:04,200 --> 00:35:07,840
You should hurry home, though.
I have a surprise for you.

382
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:26,560
Let's see here.

383
00:35:29,200 --> 00:35:31,680
This is the surprise
you were talking about?

384
00:35:32,680 --> 00:35:34,600
- Where did you buy them?
- Hey!

385
00:35:35,320 --> 00:35:38,240
That's so insulting.
I made them all myself.

386
00:35:38,320 --> 00:35:41,080
- Really?
- Yeah. Try it if you don't believe me.

387
00:35:41,160 --> 00:35:43,280
I assure you,
this time you won't spit it out.

388
00:36:03,080 --> 00:36:04,440
It really is great!

389
00:36:06,920 --> 00:36:09,120
Looks like those cooking lessons
really paid off.

390
00:36:10,360 --> 00:36:14,560
Tell me. Would you want me

391
00:36:14,640 --> 00:36:18,480
to cook every meal for you from now on?

392
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:23,480
Of course. That would be amazing.

393
00:36:24,440 --> 00:36:27,120
What about desserts?

394
00:36:28,480 --> 00:36:30,240
You know how to make them?

395
00:36:33,160 --> 00:36:35,400
I wouldn't need to take lessons for that.

396
00:36:54,920 --> 00:36:56,320
See?

397
00:36:56,960 --> 00:36:58,600
I'm the best dessert.

398
00:37:06,960 --> 00:37:09,080
Take off your glasses before you kiss me.

399
00:37:10,080 --> 00:37:11,320
They're in the way.

400
00:37:34,960 --> 00:37:38,560
We want to ask you something personal
this time. Is that okay, Ms. Neen?

401
00:37:39,400 --> 00:37:40,360
Sure.

402
00:37:40,440 --> 00:37:43,080
As we all know, you've gotten married
and divorced before.

403
00:37:43,160 --> 00:37:45,120
It had many people wondering

404
00:37:45,200 --> 00:37:47,960
how someone like you
could have a rocky relationship?

405
00:37:51,360 --> 00:37:55,720
Honestly, I think anyone
can go through a rough patch.

406
00:37:57,240 --> 00:38:01,080
Especially when it comes to
relationships or marriages, which are

407
00:38:01,160 --> 00:38:02,360
very sensitive topics.

408
00:38:02,440 --> 00:38:06,120
They're also beyond our control,
and just complicated in general.

409
00:38:07,760 --> 00:38:10,280
But things are going great now, right?

410
00:38:10,360 --> 00:38:13,040
Of course. My wife is so sweet.

411
00:38:13,120 --> 00:38:16,800
And I believe I am a sweet wife too.

412
00:38:16,880 --> 00:38:20,080
You seem so happy
when you talk about your wife.

413
00:38:20,680 --> 00:38:24,440
Of course. I'm happy
whenever I see her face.

414
00:38:24,520 --> 00:38:27,920
And I'm happy
whenever I speak of her or think of her.

415
00:38:37,960 --> 00:38:39,400
You know,

416
00:38:40,720 --> 00:38:42,600
I used to think

417
00:38:43,320 --> 00:38:46,440
marriage was about
getting people to accept us.

418
00:38:48,680 --> 00:38:51,080
But once we lost everything,

419
00:38:51,160 --> 00:38:55,080
only then I realized,
it has nothing to do with anyone.

420
00:39:01,160 --> 00:39:02,680
This time,

421
00:39:03,280 --> 00:39:05,800
I don't want to prove anything to anyone.

422
00:39:06,760 --> 00:39:08,320
I don't want to win against anyone

423
00:39:09,360 --> 00:39:11,520
or explain anything.

424
00:39:12,120 --> 00:39:14,200
I just want to ask you…

425
00:39:16,120 --> 00:39:20,160
Since you're a woman
who's learned quite a lot about love,

426
00:39:24,560 --> 00:39:27,120
will you marry me again?

427
00:40:00,880 --> 00:40:02,320
Well? Neen?

428
00:40:06,160 --> 00:40:09,440
Will you marry me again?

429
00:40:34,360 --> 00:40:35,280
Yes.

430
00:40:38,320 --> 00:40:40,000
But this time,

431
00:40:40,960 --> 00:40:43,240
it's not to prove anything to anyone.

432
00:40:46,760 --> 00:40:47,880
I'm doing it

433
00:40:49,520 --> 00:40:51,960
because my heart chooses you.

434
00:41:00,520 --> 00:41:02,120
I promise

435
00:41:03,680 --> 00:41:05,040
to love you

436
00:41:06,440 --> 00:41:08,400
and care about your feelings.

437
00:41:10,200 --> 00:41:11,440
I will be faithful.

438
00:41:14,720 --> 00:41:18,560
And I promise to stay right by your side

439
00:41:19,400 --> 00:41:21,000
through thick

440
00:41:21,960 --> 00:41:23,440
and thin.

441
00:41:25,960 --> 00:41:27,560
I love you, Neen.

442
00:41:28,840 --> 00:41:30,720
You're the only one I love.

443
00:41:31,800 --> 00:41:34,080
Forever.

444
00:41:37,520 --> 00:41:39,280
I love you too.

445
00:41:40,880 --> 00:41:42,400
You're the only one I love.

446
00:41:43,040 --> 00:41:44,680
Forever.

447
00:43:11,280 --> 00:43:15,000
My baby, don't run!

448
00:43:20,600 --> 00:43:25,040
Calm down, baby.
Mommy still hasn't prepared your food.

449
00:43:26,080 --> 00:43:28,080
How did you just refer to yourself?

450
00:43:28,160 --> 00:43:29,880
I said "Mommy."

451
00:43:29,960 --> 00:43:32,840
So what should our baby call me?

452
00:43:33,600 --> 00:43:35,280
You're her other mommy.

453
00:43:42,280 --> 00:43:43,400
Are you hungry yet?

454
00:43:44,640 --> 00:43:46,560
Are you hungry yet?

455
00:43:50,720 --> 00:43:52,520
Now

456
00:43:52,600 --> 00:43:54,920
it really feels like we're starting over.

457
00:43:57,000 --> 00:43:59,880
It's not exactly starting over.

458
00:43:59,960 --> 00:44:02,960
It's more like starting our relationship

459
00:44:03,040 --> 00:44:05,240
in the way we always wanted.

460
00:44:07,400 --> 00:44:10,760
So, it's us three taking care
of each other, right?

461
00:44:12,720 --> 00:44:16,520
Yes. This is our family.

462
00:45:34,400 --> 00:45:39,040
Subtitle translation by:
Ramil Natnitiwitaya
